Ideas, no code
--------------
Plain's design borrows ideas from these languages. No source code was copied.

- Elm (BSD-3-Clause): friendly compiler error messages, no runtime exceptions.
- Rust (MIT OR Apache-2.0): Option and Result types, the ? operator, exhaustive match.
- Gleam (Apache-2.0): a small typed language that compiles to JavaScript, one formatter style.
- Swift (Apache-2.0): optionals checked by the compiler.
- OCaml (LGPL-2.1 with linking exception): Hindley-Milner type inference, tagged unions.

Third-party code
----------------
None. The compiler uses only the Go standard library.
